hi  today we're going to solve a puzzle  called the triangle area puzzle  what we have is  four different triangles  where the hypotenuse is three  and the length of one leg is one unit  longer than the other  the question is what's the area of a  single triangle  i'm going to give you a moment to solve  this you can pause the video and take  your time  once you're ready  you can keep playing  the answer to this puzzle  is that the area of a single triangle is  two  the more interesting part is how we can  arrive at the answer  one way you can solve this is you can  work algebraically  this is the long way to solve the  problem  the steps involved are you would label  the two legs of the triangle as a and b  you can then set up a system of  equations  one equation will be that a is equal to  b plus one because we know one of the  legs is one unit longer than the other  the other equation is that a squared  plus b squared equals c squared the  hypotenuse squared  in this case three squared by the  pythagorean theorem  we now have two equations  for two unknown variables which means we  can solve for a and b  and then the final step would be to find  the area of a single triangle which is  one half a times b  this is a rather long and messy way to  solve this problem i'm actually not  going to go through the algebra  if you do you'll find out the answer is  two  however i want to point out a much more  elegant way to solve this problem which  is geometric  so what we're going to do we start out  with these same four triangles and we  can do a little neat trick where we  rearrange the triangles as follows we're  going to move one up  this one to the side and shift this one  over  now we've noticed something neat we  basically have  a big square which has  a side 3 and we have the four triangles  and we have a small square  from this we can figure out the answer  we know that the area of the big square  is equal to the area of the four  triangles plus the area of the small  square  we can solve the area of the big square  three squared  must be equal to one squared plus the  area of the four triangles  that means the area of the four  triangles must equal eight and the area  of a single triangle is two  i hope you enjoyed this puzzle please  subscribe to the channel and you can  also follow me on mind your decisions  on my blog i post weekly puzzles on  monday  there are also weekly game three posts  on tuesday  and that's my  twitter at preshtalwalker thanks for  watching

